# generated/ holds build artifacts only, never committed. data.gob is a
# //go:embed blob, deterministic from docs/, produced by `go generate ./...`
# (the release workflow runs this before building, so released binaries embed
# a fresh blob) — committing it would make doc-touching branches
# binary-conflict on it. Fresh clones must run `go generate ./...` once
# before `go build`/`go test`. The whole dir is ignored so stray local
# artifacts (e.g. an on-disk search index from an older build) can never be
# committed either.
